Don't report the tree expand/collapse key as a keyboard shortcut.

wxDataViewCtrlAccessible::GetKeyboardShortcut() returned the literal "Left" or
"Right" for an expandable tree node, i.e. the arrow key which would collapse or
expand it. The MSAA keyboard shortcut slot is meant for a real accelerator such
as "ALT+K", and screen readers append its contents to every announcement of the
element, so each row was read as e.g. "Plate 1 expanded Left". The
expanded/collapsed state is already exposed by GetState() and read out
immediately before the shortcut, so the hint adds nothing but noise.

Report no shortcut for the rows, as was already the case for the control itself.

 src/generic/datavgen.cpp | 37 +++++++++----------------------------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 28 deletions(-)

